Godzilla: Save the Earth (Xbox) - recompiled for Windows - v@VERSION@
a Replay Revival recomp                       https://replayrevival.com

EARLY ALPHA - WORK IN PROGRESS. Development continues. Expect bugs.

Not affiliated with or endorsed by Toho, Atari or Pipeworks. You must own the game.
This download contains no game files. You need your own copy of the Xbox game,
as a disc image (.iso) or an extracted folder.

WHAT YOU NEED
  - Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, a GPU with Direct3D 11.
  - Your own copy of Godzilla: Save the Earth (Xbox), as a disc image (.iso)
    or an extracted folder that contains default.xbe. An .iso is unpacked once on first use
    (about 0.8 GB of free space needed).
  - Windows "N" editions need the Media Feature Pack (the game uses Media Foundation).
  - The Visual C++ runtime DLLs are included; no separate install needed.
  - Unzip to a folder you can write to (not Program Files). The game keeps its saves and
    caches next to the program.

HOW TO START
  1. Run launcher.exe.
  2. Choose your disc image (.iso) or extracted game folder.
  3. Pick a preset (Original, Max, Low-end), adjust settings if you like, press Play.
  Your disc image or game folder is only read and never changed. An .iso is unpacked
  once into data\game\ and reused from then on.

VIDEO SETTINGS
  - Resolution starts at your screen's own (native) resolution, including ultrawide
    (21:9, 32:9). With several monitors, the Display row picks the monitor.
  - Gameplay view: "Original (4:3)" or "Fit my screen". Menus always keep their 4:3 shape.
  - V-Sync is On by default (no tearing). Variable refresh rate is Auto and needs
    FreeSync/G-Sync enabled on your monitor and graphics driver.
  - If the game stops, the launcher tells you what happened and offers "Try again with
    original settings" (your saved settings are not changed), "Try borderless instead",
    the log folder, and a Copy details button for bug reports.
    After a crash it can also save a crash report zip to your desktop for you to send.

MODS
  - The Mods tab installs a mod from a .zip or a folder (or drag it onto the launcher window),
    turns mods on and off, sets their load order and removes them. Mods live in data\mods\.
    Your game files are never changed. Removed mods are moved to data\mods\_removed\.
  - A mod made for a different version of the game is marked and skipped.

WHERE THINGS GO (this download runs portable)
  saves\          the game's save data (starts empty, like a new console)
  shadercache\    compiled shaders (created on first start; the first start is slower)
  data\           launcher settings, the ini files it passes to the game, mods, and logs
  data\game\      the unpacked copy of your disc, if you chose an .iso (about 0.8 GB)
  Delete these folders to reset (deleting data\ means an .iso is unpacked again and mods are gone).

CONTROLS
  Keyboard: arrows = d-pad, Enter = Start, Backspace = Back, Z X C V = A B X Y,
  Q / E = White / Black, 1 / 3 = triggers, W A S D / I J K L = sticks.
  Gamepads work (Xbox tested; PlayStation, Switch and generic pads untested). The
  launcher's Controllers tab shows connected pads and lets you set dead zone, rumble and
  button mapping, and which button names the game shows (Button prompts: Auto, Xbox,
  Original Xbox, PlayStation). The game reads these when it starts.
  Black = left shoulder, White = right shoulder.

IN-GAME MENU
  Hold Back and Start together for a second on any controller (or press F1, or the Guide button) to pause the game and
  open the menu: volume, mouse pointer and the other settings, controller setup, Return to launcher and Quit. Volume and
  the mouse pointer change at once; Button prompts and the enhancements apply from the next match; the rest from the
  next start. The menu needs ste_overlay.dll next to the game program.

KNOWN ISSUES (alpha)
  - Some distant buildings still pop in and out in a few places.
  - Mechagodzilla 3's back missiles are invisible while they fly (the launch flash and the hits show).
  - Typing a profile name with the keyboard is not possible yet.
  - Windows only; Linux and Mac are untested.
  - Only Xbox controllers have been tested so far.

BUG REPORTS
  https://github.com/replayrevival/ste-recomp/issues
  Include your Windows version, GPU, and what you did before the problem happened.
  When the launcher shows "The game stopped", press Copy details and paste it into the report.

